From 8aca22f61ef668cc57868b420d9af91534edca3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 15:29:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0143 -- wave-48 H-A skip-when-unchanged
 backdrop

Per flush-instr's WAVE-47-V1-LOG-ANALYSIS sec. 6 recommendation: H-A
backdrop dominance was confirmed via wave-47 v1 mds-bg sub-decomp
diagnostic at canonical Mimiga BK_PARALLAX scene (backdrop = 5.4 ms /
57% of mds_tilemap_bg parent; 4.18 ms / 51% averaged across multi-
scene TAS). Predicted savings -2 to -4 ms / flip = +1.5 to +3 fps on
the wave-46 28.85 fps baseline.

LEVER MECHANISM: memoize the BG scroll-state tuple (curmap,
backdrop_id, scrolltype, displayed_xscroll, displayed_yscroll,
flipacceltime_nonzero, _cached_window_surface ptr, direct-VESA gen)
across frames. When the current frame's tuple matches the last
successfully-drawn frame AND killswitch is not engaged AND not in
flipacceltime mode, skip BOTH clearScreen(BLACK) and
map_draw_backdrop() entirely. The window surface's BG-visible
regions retain pixels from the previous frame's draw; subsequent
FG-tilelayer + sprite + textbox passes write over their own regions
normally (FG draws are NOT skipped -- only the per-frame BG
preservation is memoized).

SCOPE EXPANSION FROM ORIGINAL BRIEF: flush-instr's WAVE-47-V1
sec. 6.1 framed the lever as "scope to BK_PARALLAX branch in
map_draw_backdrop." nx-engine audit found this scope was load-
bearing-incorrect: skipping only the backdrop blit leaves the
window's BG-visible regions BLACK because Renderer::clearScreen runs
unconditionally at game.cpp:DrawScene line 666-669 BEFORE
map_draw_backdrop, blanking the full 320x240 surface every frame
via patch 0058's memset16 fast path. Patch 0071 (wave 15) explicitly
removed the earlier fingerprint-skip mechanism. For Mimiga
BK_PARALLAX scenes with substantial sky regions (FG doesn't cover
them), skipping only the backdrop produces visible black-sky
regression -- a ship-blocking correctness bug, not a subtle issue.

Team-lead ack'd scope expansion to DrawScene: skip BOTH the
clearScreen AND map_draw_backdrop atomically via a single skip-state
helper. LOC budget went 30-50 -> ~70 (within the 50-80 expanded
band).

SUPERSEDES PARTIAL-SKIP BEHAVIOR OF PATCHES 0080/0126: those patches
implement a backdrop tile-loop cache (skip the tile loop on cache
HIT; render direct-to-window on thrashing miss). On cache HIT they
STILL issue drawCachedBackdrop (cache->window blit). The 5.4 ms
flush-instr measured at Mimiga BK_PARALLAX IS that blit (plus the
clearScreen it has to undo). Patch 0143 layers ON TOP of 0080/0126:
when the scroll-state key matches AND last present succeeded, we
skip BOTH the clearScreen AND the entire map_draw_backdrop call --
including the cache-HIT blit that 0080/0126's HIT path still pays.
The pre-existing cache machinery continues to handle the cache-MISS
case (player motion changes parscroll -> cache MISS -> tile-loop
render into cache -> blit cache to window) which is when state IS
changing and the BG must be redrawn. NOT a refactor of 0080/0126
(scope-creep avoided); just a stronger early-out at the caller.

Regenerated from current vendor state to fix patch context drift
(team-lead's ASCII-cleanup substitution broke the original patch's
context-line matching; source content unchanged; this re-emits a
byte-exact patch against the current upstream context).

Banner regex for tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS:
"map: BG skip-when-unchanged (ENABLED|DISABLED)"
"bg-skip: (first event|backdrop redraw skipped)"
